<title>Solo friendly auction</title>
<description>I need to give some games a new home and a fresh start!   This is my first auction, so bear with me please.  😀   Thank you to various people who have knowingly or unknowingly helped me with the rules below.

Auction rules:

1. All bids must be in whole dollars, starting with the listed "starting" bid.  Any bids below the minimum bid will not be considered.  Please consider your bid to be a commitment to buy the item at that price (+shipping) should you win the item.  If you are not certain you want to buy the item at your bid price, please wait to bid until you are.

2.  Any item without bids may have its minimum and BIN prices changed or be withdrawn from the auction.

3.  I will do my best to give an accurate description of the game condition.   I will note any damage that is noticeable to me. Unless the game is described as "like new" or better, do expect some minor wear on the boxes and rulebooks.  I often discard inserts in favor of bags or plastic container boxes for better organization.   The games are in a non-smoking home.

4.  Please use the comments at the bottom of the list for questions or discussion and reply to individual items only to place bids.

5. Please try to include your ZIP in your bid so I can estimate costs once the auction ends.

6. Local pickup is available in Medina, OH.

7. Shipping is from 44256 if you'd like to estimate beforehand.  All shipping will be paid by the item's winner.  If you win multiple items, I'll do my best to ship in one box.  I will use Pirate Ship and will ship to USA addresses only.

8. All shipping transactions will be conducted via Zelle, Venmo, or PayPal.  If you are doing local pickup, I prefer cash.  All sales will go through the marketplace so that BGG gets its cut.

9. The auction will run until 9:00PM EST Saturday, November 8th.  To prevent "sniping", if any item receives bids within the last hour of the auction ending time, that item will have its ending time extended for another hour from that bid time.  This will keep rolling if the bidding war continues over a particular item (although the rest of the auction will close.)    The winning bid will be the last one within an hour of the previous one in this case, if that makes sense.  Obviously, a BIN bid will end it.

10.  If you bid BIN, I will try to get your game out before the end of the auction, but I can't promise it.   Edit:  If you aren't going to bid on additional games and/or want your BIN early, note that in your bid.

If you have any questions, please send me a geekmail!    Happy bidding  😀</description>

